[0.569,"o","\u001b[H\r\u001b[6B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mPlease implement this issue.\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m#26 The summary of one month\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mAt the end of each month accounting closes the books, and wants the summary of the \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231minvoices issued in that month. Add \u001b[38;5;153m--month <YYYY-MM>\u001b[38;5;231m to \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer summary\u001b[38;5;231m: with it, the \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231msummary covers only the invoices issued in that month, such as \u001b[38;5;153m--month 2026-10\u001b[38;5;231m.\u001b[39m         \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m- Without \u001b[38;5;153m--month\u001b[38;5;231m, the summary prints exactly what it prints today.\u001b[39m                     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m- A month not written as YYYY-MM is an error that names it.\u001b[39m                             \r\u001b[13B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;174m✽\u001b[3GHatching… \r\u001b[3B\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
